{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDIyL0JleW9uZCUyMFRoZSUyMFdhc3RlbGFuZCUyMCUyODIwMjIlMjkv","type":"movie","name":"Beyond The Wasteland","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/wE1A9fQFP9BhTXbP4lsPfDUR1tt.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/lIiBX2XCZyidq7QdQwIcohmCUJV.jpg","description":"Shot in Australia, USA, Italy, France, Germany, and Japan, Beyond the Wasteland follows the fans from around the world who go to extraordinary lengths in the name of Mad Max. Transporting us into the world of Mad Max, we explore the eccentric world of the fans, their costumes, and their machines as these oddball fans find their place amongst the Mad Max community.  The documentary also follows original cast member, Bertrand Cadart as he continues his fight against stage IV leukemia and travels from his home on the Sunshine Coast to the “Wasteland,” the desert location of Mad Max 2 in Silverton, for the last time. Beyond the Wasteland not only celebrates life but the ability to change oneself through passion.\n\nRated 12 · Released 5 Feb 2022 · Australia · Language: English · 93 min\nStudio: The Picture Lot\n\nOn your server — Audio: English · Subtitle files: English","releaseInfo":"2022","genres":["Documentary","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"6.0","runtime":"93 min","cast":["Roger Ward","Bertrand Cadart","Paul Johnstone","Jared Butler","Alan Finney","Jim 'Tank' Dorsey"],"director":["Eddie Beyrouthy"],"released":"2022-02-05T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"It's more than a film. It's a way of life.","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Eddie Beyrouthy","character":"Director"},{"name":"Roger Ward","character":"Self","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/1ABctS3WpNwqlSzytPwudMSrIge.jpg"},{"name":"Bertrand Cadart","character":"Self"},{"name":"Paul Johnstone","character":"Self"},{"name":"Jared Butler","character":"Self"},{"name":"Alan Finney","character":"Self","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/aXIKINajg3w2lWl5yiSCLr3mC1G.jpg"},{"na